            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a delicious drink - very tasty and thirst-quenching, but the recipe needed some adjustment. When scaled to one serving only 2T rum was called for in a pint of soda. I just used the measurements listed as a guideline. What I did: a large water glass, 4 ice cubes, a shot of rum, 2T grenadine, 1/4 lime, juiced; and then filled the glass with lime soda. You could not taste the rum at all and it was very delicious."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "WillTA3"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made it as Evening Pitcher Drink....\nCut down the Grenadine as suggested by most of the review...\n\nI went 3 to 1 Rum to Grenadine\n6 Fresh limes squeezed, 2 sliced and tossed in the pitcher. Matched 7up to Rum/Grenadine lime in the Pitcher, served over Ice.\n\nWas Excellent... Crowd Favorite so far... So good, I forgot to take a Picture!",
            "datePublished": "2020-06-10T14:58:48.783Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Craig Patchett"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Not a Cherry Bomb! Swap the rum for Cachaça, the grenadine for a good cherry liqueur, the lime soda for club soda, and throw the maraschino cherries in the trash and you have a true Cherry Bomb. This had way too much sugar as well.",
            "datePublished": "2024-02-22T22:23:01.837Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CASSANDRA"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was better with twice the amount of rum, which cut the sweetness to an acceptable level. We poured these over shaved ice which added to the refreshing quality.",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-26T11:08:42.847Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Angela Christensen Baker"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't have grenadine on hand or maraschino cherries so I used homemade amaretto cherries and the juice from the cherries. Super good!",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-30T20:38:12.963Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mike Bogan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This drink was okay, but you can make it better. Following the recipe, we couldn't even taste the alcohol. So you definitely want to double the rum to at least 8oz....10oz was even better.",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-19T23:24:48.037Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kati Stafford"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have been making something similar... I call it cherry limeade- instead of regular rum I use cherry rum and just a splash of grenadine",
            "datePublished": "2015-06-03T04:01:40.157Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SaltyJenn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved this as written! We didn't think it was too syrupy. But you may want to halve the grenadine and work your way up just to be certain. :) Oh, and be careful with these! We couldn't taste the rum...at all!!! It hit me after about the 4th one. lol.",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-15T10:30:08.037Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "chester"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yum! Made this over the weekend of the Fourth and used Sierra Mist soda, which would be the only thing I change for the next time - that soda tends to taste flat sooner than most. I actually took the cherries and marinated them in vodka prior to garnishing the drinks with them. Everyone got a nice POP once they were to the end of the drink. I also halved the amount of grenadine per the advice of others.",
            "datePublished": "2003-07-07T16:30:39.873Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "IMVINTAGE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This tastes EXACTLY like a cherry limeade ( &amp; I'm an expert on the subject!) I did cut wayyy back on the grenadine...I don't think it needs more than an ounce &amp; a half.",
            "datePublished": "2006-05-28T07:36:40.780Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "1"
